From a0ca65efdd790627acde96fe9923d8c9e7fb56f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:33:21 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 37/60] MiMo-V2: an 8-bit key/value cache for the
 full-attention layers, --policy kv=fp8

`--policy kv=fp8` keeps the keys and values of MiMo's 9 full-attention layers in e4m3 with an fp32 scale a token and
key head (absmax / 448). A decode step at long context reads half the bytes; the sliding layers keep 16 bits.
`kv=fp16`, the 16-bit cache, stays the default and the exact path; the 8-bit cache is not bit-equal to it.

- kv8.cu: RoPE and quantise on write (mimo_qkv8), decode attention over the 8-bit tiles with two stages in flight,
  1,024 keys a program (mimo_rows8), the fold (mimo_merge8), and a dequantise for the prompt kernel, which keeps
  reading fp16 keys of the slot.
- kv8.zig: the cache's scales and launches; the model allocates the 8-bit keys and values in its own caches.
- Rank 0 announces the cache in its hello, so `tf-mimo follow` builds the same model.
- native/cuda.zig serves --policy for families that take one and shows the active policy on /health.
- `tf-mimo kv8check MODEL AOT_DIR`: the 8-bit decode attention against Triton's on the same values and on the
  16-bit ones, rows at position 128,000.

(cherry picked from commit 83fd3f2d66df138d7c0a163ccc02c5b2faf0e83c)
